      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 1,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": null,
      "index": "a6",
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 1920554074,
      "version": 743,
      "versionNonce": 1622603206,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": null,
      "updated": 1753756444254,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "It will do this by looping through a generator.\nThis generator will be a custom generator, and\nwon't work exactly like a generator, but will be\nsimilar.\n\nIt will have a \"next\" function, that has an\noptions object that will contain options for the\nline that it returns.\n\nWhen it runs out of lines to provide, it will return\nNone, indicating the end of the list.\n\nHowever, it won't just act as a generator. It will\nalso act as the class to append the output to.\nSince it is managing the tabination, it will keep\ntrack of the current list we are appending to,\nand it will add the new lines to it.",
      "fontSize": 20,
      "fontFamily": 5,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": "qpXoBy0_a0XQ1otuMXb-9",
      "originalText": "It will do this by looping through a generator. This generator will be a custom generator, and won't work exactly like a generator, but will be similar.\n\nIt will have a \"next\" function, that has an options object that will contain options for the line that it returns.\n\nWhen it runs out of lines to provide, it will return None, indicating the end of the list.\n\nHowever, it won't just act as a generator. It will also act as the class to append the output to. Since it is managing the tabination, it will keep track of the current list we are appending to, and it will add the new lines to it.",
      "autoResize": true,
      "lineHeight": 1.25
    }
  ],
